cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use SpinSpec to simulate or analyze NMR spectra in a scientific
  publication, thesis, or presentation, please cite this software.
type: software
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-27
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23696822
title: "SpinSpec: Quantum simulation of NMR spectra"
authors:
  - family-names: Kupriyanov
    given-names: Pavel
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6610-2785"
abstract: >-
  SpinSpec computes transition frequencies and relative spectral intensities
  for coupled spin-1/2 nuclear magnetic resonance systems by constructing
  and diagonalizing the spin Hamiltonian, with Zeeman and scalar J couplings.
repository-code: "https://github.com/scleroze/SpinSpec"
url: "https://nmrspec.org"
keywords:
  - nuclear magnetic resonance
  - NMR simulation
  - J coupling
  - spin Hamiltonian
  - Earth's magnetic field
